From 3178baeba6cf1c6f6a70cde0272ae934f514f503 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 05:48:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix drip lock: read Firestore Timestamp registration date

Students are saved with a Firestore Timestamp, but the drip code did
arithmetic on the raw value, so exercises could fail to lock.

- add timestampToMs() (Timestamp, {_seconds}, Date, ISO string, number)
- use it in evaluateExerciseAvailability and the student portal
- getDripUnlockMs returns early on a non-finite date instead of looping
- tests cover every date shape, a missing date and NaN
---
 scripts/test-student-access.mjs | 22 ++++++++++++++++++
 src/lib/studentAccess.ts        | 40 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 src/lib/studentServer.ts        |  4 ++--
 3 files changed, 61 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/scripts/test-student-access.mjs b/scripts/test-student-access.mjs
index aa61f64..b4ddfd0 100644
--- a/scripts/test-student-access.mjs
